  "description": "Seasonal Contrast (SeCo) is a self-supervised pre-training pipeline for remote sensing imagery that leverages unlabeled, uncurated Sentinel-2 data and a multi-augmentation contrastive learning method to learn representations that are both variant and invariant to seasonal changes. SeCo achieves state-of-the-art results on land-cover classification and change detection tasks.",
